-- title:
--   Reduced q-expansion function field generated by integral chart functions
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a positive integer with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume $M/p$ is nonzero; let `hj` be a proof that the Laurent series $j = q^{-1}\cdot\sum$ (the series `jqModC` $\mathbb{Q}$) lies in $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb{Q}\ \top$, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the ratios $p_f/p_g$ of the $q$-expansions of pairs of modular forms of equal weight and full level having integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ with $p_g \neq 0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), whose residue field $\kappa_A$ has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed. Then the analogous field $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa_A\ (\mathrm{\Gamma N}\ p\ M\ H)$ inside $\kappa_A((q))$, generated over $\kappa_A$ by the ratios of the $\kappa_A$-coefficient reductions of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight on the congruence subgroup $\mathrm{\Gamma N}\ p\ M\ H$ of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, is contained in the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $\kappa_A$ all series of the form $x =$ the coefficientwise reduction modulo the maximal ideal of some $y \in A((q))$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ is the $q$-expansion of an element $b$ of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin` at level $\mathrm{\Gamma N}\ p\ M\ H$, that is, of an element of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ at that level which is integral over the subalgebra generated by $j$ over the coefficient ring $R\ p$.
--
--   This is the generation half of the $q$-expansion principle at the level prime to $p$: the function field of the reduced curve over $\kappa_A$ is generated by reductions of those chart functions whose $q$-expansions admit coefficientwise $A$-integral lifts; the reverse inclusion is not asserted. It is used in the analysis of the integral model at $p$, where the reduction of the reading-off map on the special fibre is identified.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRLevel_qExpFunctionFieldC_residueField_le_adjoin_coeffMap_residue_of_mem_chartAlgFin.lean

